  <div class="content-section">
    <h2>What is Keyboard Latency?</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard latency is the delay between pressing a key and the signal being
      registered by your system. For everyday typing it is imperceptible, but in
      competitive gaming even a few milliseconds can affect your performance.
    </p>
    <h2 style="margin-top:2rem;">How is Keyboard Latency Calculated?</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard latency is the sum of three delays that happen between your
      finger pressing a key and the character appearing on screen. Here's a
      real-world example:
    </p>
    <div
      class="callout"
      style="background: var(--bg2); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem; margin: 1.25rem 0; font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--text2); line-height: 1.75;"
    >
      <strong>Example calculation:</strong><br />
      5ms (key debounce time) + 1ms (polling rate) + 5ms (system latency) = <strong
        style="color: var(--accent);">11ms total latency</strong
      >
    </div>
    <p>
      <strong>Note on scan rate:</strong> This tool measures your <strong
        >fastest recorded key-press duration</strong
      >, not your keyboard's actual hardware scan rate. Scan rate is a fixed
      property of the keyboard's internal controller (typically 1000Hz or
      higher) and can't be reliably derived from how long you hold a key. What
      this number <em>is</em> useful for: comparing keys against each other, or spotting
      one key that's noticeably slower than the rest.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:2rem;">How to Test Your Keyboard Latency</h2>
    <ol
      style="color: var(--text2); font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.85; padding-left: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;"
    >
      <li>Scroll up to the keyboard tester above.</li>
      <li>
        Press any key on your physical keyboard — it will highlight instantly on
        screen.
      </li>
      <li>
        Each press logs its response time in the Key Press History section.
      </li>
      <li>
        Your shortest press time and estimated scan rate update live at the top.
      </li>
      <li>
        Test multiple keys to get a reliable average — then compare against the
        table below.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <div class="info-grid">
      <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-icon">⚡</div><div class="info-card-title">
          Scan Rate
        </div><div class="info-card-desc">
          How many times per second the keyboard's controller scans for key
          presses (a fixed hardware spec — not something this browser tool can
          measure directly).
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-icon">📡</div><div class="info-card-title">
          Polling Rate
        </div><div class="info-card-desc">
          How often the keyboard reports data to your PC. Standard is 1000Hz
          (1ms). Gaming keyboards reach 8000Hz.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-icon">⏱</div><div class="info-card-title">
          Response Time
        </div><div class="info-card-desc">
          Total delay from key press to on-screen action — scan rate plus
          polling rate plus system latency combined.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-icon">🔌</div><div class="info-card-title">
          Connection Type
        </div><div class="info-card-desc">
          Wired USB has the lowest latency. Modern 2.4GHz wireless nearly
          matches wired. Bluetooth adds 10–30ms extra.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
